      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1776095941303,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "\"Distributed Monolith\" - You think getting a bunch of developers in the same solution in sync\nis hard, trying doing that across the company.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "\"Distributed Monolith\" - You think getting a bunch of developers in the same solution in sync\nis hard, trying doing that across the company.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "-HNgtbTS7mf2JRbccTmHG",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 424,
      "y": 1240,
      "width": 876.679443359375,
      "height": 250,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "aJ",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1776539579,
      "version": 471,
      "versionNonce": 32264571,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1776097054994,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "- Services, in order to be \"independently deployable\" have one huge obstacle.\n    - they can't depend on things they don't own.\n    - most commonly that is a database.\n    - therefore the ONE rule I will say about \"is this a microservice or not\" isn't size, etc.\n        MICROSERVICES DON'T SHARE DATABASES\n\nour goal - \n    - our service will provide consistent value across deployments.\n    - we will minimize our dependency on outside services that can break our service.\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "- Services, in order to be \"independently deployable\" have one huge obstacle.\n    - they can't depend on things they don't own.\n    - most commonly that is a database.\n    - therefore the ONE rule I will say about \"is this a microservice or not\" isn't size, etc.\n        MICROSERVICES DON'T SHARE DATABASES\n\nour goal - \n    - our service will provide consistent value across deployments.\n    - we will minimize our dependency on outside services that can break our service.\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
